    "knowledge_point_id": "65f742e7-89c6-543b-b43a-f41c27f35abf",
    "knowledge_point": "Finding the General Solution of a Singular 3x3 System of Equations with One Pivot",
    "problem": "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -6 & 4 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 9 & -6 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix.",
    "worked_solution": "Reducing $M$ to echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -6 & 4 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 9 & -6 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=-{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -6 & 4 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 9 & -6 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 9 & -6 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-3y+2z=-1 \\\\ 0x+0y+0z=0 \\\\ 0x+0y+0z=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince any numbers $x,y,z$ form a solution of the final two equations $0x+0y+0z=0,$ we can remove these equations from the system. So, our system now consists of just a single equation:\n\n$$\nx-3y+2z=-1\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variable is $x$, and we have two free variables $y$ and $z.$ That means we need to find $x$ in terms of $y,z.$ Doing this, we get\n\n$$\nx=3y-2z-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=3y-2z-1 \\\\ y=y \\\\ z=z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $y,z$ (the free variables) are arbitrary numbers.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3y-2z-1 \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
